& [Stages]
  + AC1 compile one inert exact activation proposal
  + AC2 independently verify proposal bytes published lineage and producer-plan reconstruction
  + AC3 accept one externally supplied explicit authorize or reject decision
  + AC4 independently admit decision identity signature nonce freshness scope and ceilings
  + AC5 mint at most one private affine permit only for admitted_authorize
  + AC6 consume that permit before entering the existing runner exactly once
  + AC7 independently replay the runner receipt and effect account
  + AC8 seal exactly one terminal record and permanently close the ceremony
  + predecessor edges are AC1 none AC2 AC1 AC3 AC2 AC4 AC3 AC5 AC4 AC6 AC5 AC7 AC6 AC8 AC7 except admitted_reject or any typed refusal closes directly at AC8 without inventing skipped outputs

& [DecisionAuthority]
  + continuation work-slice language publication successful tests fixture success prior ceremony artifacts or model inference are never decisions
  + decision binds ceremony and proposal digests operator principal role subject nonce issue time not-before expiration authorize-or-reject attempt1 permit1 process1 retry0 and exact effect ceiling
  + current time signature custody and operator identity verification are separately supplied observations and cannot be synthesized by the compiler
  + absent malformed unverifiable mismatched not-yet-valid expired replayed or ambiguous decision closes refused with no permit

& [PermitConservation]
  + private permit has no Serialize Deserialize Clone Copy Default public field public constructor persistent form recovery path or transfer representation
  + AC5 exchanges one admitted authorization for one permit and cannot mint on reject or refusal
  + AC6 irreversibly consumes before runner entry; spawn failure timeout truncation nonzero exit executable drift provider-unavailable and downstream refusal do not return replace or refresh it
  + attempts1 permits1 processes1 retries0 and no terminal state has an outgoing transition

& [Receipts]
  + runner receipt must bind exact before-and-after executable digest process record observation verification total processes1 active terminal0 resume count1 single-use consumed true provider requests0 remote calls1 effects1
  + ceremony receipt binds proposal decision admission permit consumption runner receipt and a disposition without altering runner truth
  + terminal dispositions are completed_available completed_provider_unavailable rejected refused expired abandoned_after_consumption and receipt_refused
  + provider-unavailable preserves zero synthetic trials and authorizes no provider repair download install fallback or build commission

